        <h2>About kidney cancer</h2>
        <p>Kidney cancer develops when abnormal cells grow in the kidneys, the organs responsible for filtering waste from the blood. The most common type is renal cell carcinoma, although several other forms can occur. Kidney cancer may not cause noticeable symptoms early on, but signs can include blood in the urine, pain near the ribs or hips, fatigue, loss of appetite or an abdominal mass.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

