        <h2>Why choose us for kidney cancer care?</h2>
        <p>At Mays Cancer Center, home to UT Health San Antonio MD Anderson Cancer Center, our doctors are at the forefront of kidney cancer care. Our surgeons are experts at treating the most advanced kidney cancers, including technical procedures like surgery for tumor thrombus (extension of kidney cancer into the major veins) - always with a focus on you.</p>
        <p>Our skilled doctors use leading techniques to treat a high volume of kidney cancers. South Texas has a very high incidence rate of kidney cancer compared to the national average. Our team has developed advanced surgical protocols to provide exceptional cancer care close to your support network and the comforts of home.</p>

        <h3>Highlights of our kidney cancer care include:</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Specialized GU cancer expertise:</strong> Kidney cancer is a kind of genitourinary (GU) cancer, and our team includes specialists from our nationally renowned <a href="#">genitourinary cancer program</a>.</li>
          <li><strong>High-volume kidney cancer care:</strong> South Texas has higher rates of kidney cancer than most areas of the country, and our doctors treat a high volume of early and advanced kidney cancers.</li>
          <li><strong>Advanced surgical protocols:</strong> Our surgeons regularly perform complex procedures for kidney cancer that has spread beyond the kidney, including tumor thrombus surgery.</li>
          <li><strong>Team-based treatment planning:</strong> For complex cases, cancer surgeons work closely with vascular and cardiac surgeons to remove cancer while protecting nearby organs.</li>
          <li><strong>Research-informed treatment options:</strong> Our doctors have special expertise in immunotherapy and other targeted medicines that are changing kidney cancer care.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

